# GHSA-4g2h-vm7x-747c / EEF-CVE-2026-28809 / esaml XXE
#
# The advisory is in esaml's own XML decoding (esaml_sp / esaml_util), which
# web-ng never calls. esaml is a direct dependency only for :xmerl_dsig
# signature verification, and every document it sees -- SAML responses and IdP
# metadata alike -- is parsed first by
# lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_xml.ex with `dtd: :none`, which rejects
# any entity declaration and never fetches an external resource. Covered by
# test/phoenix/auth/saml_response_test.exs and saml_metadata_test.exs.
#
# There is no newer Hex release than esaml 4.6.0 available to upgrade to
# (re-verified 2026-09-25 via mix hex.info), so we track the advisory here until
# upstream publishes a patched package or the dependency is replaced.
GHSA-4g2h-vm7x-747c

# EEF-CVE-2026-93471 / esaml unbounded SAMLResponse decompression
#
# The inflate is in esaml_binding:decode_response/2, which web-ng never calls.
# The ACS accepts only the HTTP-POST binding and base64-decodes the form value
# itself (lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_response.ex); nothing in web-ng
# inflates a received SAML message. esaml is used only for :xmerl_dsig.
EEF-CVE-2026-93471

# EEF-CVE-2026-86696 / esaml atom creation from LogoutResponse status codes
#
# The atom is minted by esaml:status_code_map/1, reached only through
# esaml:decode_logout_response/1 and esaml:decode_response/1 from esaml_sp and
# esaml_cowboy. web-ng calls none of them and has no single-logout endpoint; it
# reads the response itself with XPath and never maps a StatusCode to an atom.
EEF-CVE-2026-86696

# EEF-CVE-2026-105270 / esaml atom creation while parsing SAML messages
#
# The vulnerable parse is esaml_binding:decode_response/2, which web-ng never
# calls. web-ng's own response parser had the same exposure, because
# :xmerl_scan interns every name it reads; it no longer interns any name from a
# received response: SAMLXml.parse_response/1
# (lib/serviceradar_web_ng_web/auth/saml_xml.ex) scans the document with
# :xmerl_sax_parser first and rejects any name it does not already hold as an
# atom. Covered by "interns no atom from the names in a response" in
# test/phoenix/auth/saml_response_test.exs.
EEF-CVE-2026-105270

